{"type":"message_update","assistantMessageEvent":{"type":"text_end","contentIndex":1,"content":"Fixed in `/workspace/in/csvtool`.\n\nChanged:\n- `csvtool/cli.py`\n  - Switched CSV I/O to `csv.DictReader` / `csv.DictWriter`. No line-splitting.\n  - Added `--where` repeat support via `action=\"append\"` and AND semantics.\n  - Added `normalize_argv()` so `--sort -created_at` parses as data, not as a flag.\n  - Added field validation for `--where`, `--select`, `--sort`.\n  - Added numeric-aware sort keys with descending support for `-field`.\n  - Preserved selected headers on empty result sets.\n  - Emitted clear non-zero errors for invalid `--where` and missing fields.\n\n- `csvtool/filtering.py`\n  - `parse_where()` now validates `field=value`.\n  - Added `compile_predicates()` for AND-combined filtering.\n  - `select_fields()` now indexes required fields directly instead of silently filling blanks.\n\n- `tests/test_cli_regression.py`\n  - Added regressions for:\n    - repeated `--where` AND semantics\n    - quoted comma preservation in selected output\n    - numeric descending sort\n    - invalid `--where` failure\n    - missing field failures for filter/select/sort\n\nKey check:\n- Direct CLI scenario now works:\n  - `python3 -m csvtool.cli samples/orders.csv --where status=paid --select id,total --sort -created_at`\n  - Output observed:\n    ```\n    id,total\n    o1,1200\n    o3,750\n    ```\n\nVerification:\n- Attempted requested command `python -m pytest tests` from the project dir. Failed here because `python` is not installed in this harness.\n- Attempted `python3 -m pytest tests`. Failed here because `pytest` is not installed in this harness.\n- Ran all test functions from `tests/test_cli_existing.py` and `tests/test_cli_regression.py` manually under `python3`, including `tmp_path`-based cases. Observed result:\n  - `manual test execution passed`\n\nConstraint status:\n- Did not modify `tests/test_cli_existing.py`.\n- No external deps added.\n- No hard-coded sample fixture paths.\n- CSV parsing/writing uses stdlib `csv`, not `split(\",\")`."}}
